course: dictionary
lesson: 9217
title: Solve: finding the answer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To solve something means to find the answer to it, or the way to make it right. A problem, a mystery, a puzzle, a riddle and a sum can all be solved. «Each new kind of transport solved a problem of the one before.» Each new kind of transport found a way to fix a problem the older kind had.
explain: In a mystery, solving means finding out what really happened. Detectives use clues to do this. In maths, solve is an instruction: work out the answer and check it. Solve 3 × ? = 12 and the answer is 4, because 3 × 4 = 12.
explain: You can also solve arguments with friends by talking about them. Words like problem-solving and solve for x come from the same idea. Ask yourself: what is the problem, and what would fix it?
fact: Solve is a verb. Its other forms are solves, solved and solving.
fact: To solve a problem is to find the answer to it or the way to make it right.
fact: To solve a mystery or crime is to find out what really happened.
fact: To solve a puzzle, riddle or equation is to work out its answer.
fact: «An invention is a new thing or a new way of doing something that solves a problem.»
exercise: «Each new kind of transport solved a problem of the one before.» What does solved mean here? | Made a new problem | Asked a question about the problem | Forgot the problem | *Found a way to fix a problem
exercise: The detective wants to solve the mystery. What is she trying to do? | Cook a meal | Hide the clues | *Find out what really happened | Buy a new coat
exercise: Solve 3 × ? = 12. What is the missing number? | 15 | 9 | 3 | *4
test: «Pigs learn names, solve puzzles and in one study even steered a joystick.» What does solve puzzles mean? | Sell them to other people | *Work out the answers to them | Throw them away | Break them into pieces
test: Mia and Sam keep arguing about the game. What is a good way to solve the argument? | Ignore each other forever | Tell everyone else to take sides | *Talk it through and find an answer you both accept | Shout louder until one gives up
exam: «An invention is a new thing or a new way of doing something that solves a problem.» What does solves mean here? | *Fixes the problem or finds the answer to it | Copies the problem onto paper | Makes the problem worse | Hides the problem from everyone
